.TH Y5.COMPOSITOR.SETTINGS 1 "July 2026" "y5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
y5.compositor.settings \- configuration editor for the Y5 compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B y5.compositor.settings
.RB [ \-\-write\-default ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B y5.compositor.settings
authors the complete settings file the Y5 compositor requires
.RI ( ~/.config/y5.compositor/settings.json ).
Run without arguments it opens an interactive terminal editor seeded
from the existing file, or from the canonical defaults when none
exists. Every field of the schema is always written, so the resulting
file is guaranteed complete and valid.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-write\-default
Non-interactive: write the canonical default settings and exit. Used by
the session wrapper to seed the configuration on the first start.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/y5.compositor/settings.json
The settings file, honouring
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
Changes take effect at the next compositor launch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR y5.compositor (1)
